DaPermissionHost: confirm every push_content, not only type=file

actrule.yaml lists push_content as ask, but the scene hook approved every type
except file before the policy was consulted, so a Markdown or table card reached
the user with no confirmation (kb-suite SEC-F2: a made-up interview record was
written and pushed without any prompt). push_content now goes through the policy
like the other self-guarded tools: ask -> the user confirms, allow -> it runs,
deny -> it is refused. The tool card says so.

Cost: one confirmation per pushed card. A host without an approval channel
(Swarm team member mode) denies the push, so the model answers in text instead.

Applied by deploy/compose/da/build.sh until settled upstream (agent-solution
common). Made against solution b70a00246, the deployed baseline (build with
DA_SOLUTION_REF=b70a00246; 0002 does not apply to newer common either). Newer
common keeps the auto-approval as FEAT-109's "fast path" (isFastPathShape):
rebasing means dropping the push_content shape there.

